@* In-app help. A self-contained modal (Visible + OnClose, like AgentSettingsDialog).
   Backdrop-click and the X both dismiss. *@

@if (Visible)
{
    <div class="help-backdrop" @onclick="Close">
        <div class="help-panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="ClaudeWorkbench help" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <header class="help-head">
                <div class="help-title">
                    <h2>ClaudeWorkbench --Basic &mdash; Help</h2>
                    <p>Plain Claude with all of its tools &mdash; every action needs your OK.</p>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="help-close" @onclick="Close" aria-label="Close help">&times;</button>
            </header>

            <div class="help-body">
                <section class="help-rule">
                    <strong>The one rule:</strong> Claude never acts silently. Every tool call &mdash;
                    editing a file, running a command, fetching a page &mdash; <b>pauses for your
                    Allow or Deny</b> before it runs. Nothing is injected into Claude's prompt;
                    this shell is stock Claude plus a permission gate.
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3>How a turn works</h3>
                    <ol class="help-steps">
                        <li><b>Prompt</b> in the composer and Submit Turn.</li>
                        <li>Claude answers, or reaches for a tool &mdash; each call pops the <b>Allow / Deny</b> dialog.</li>
                        <li>If Claude asks <em>you</em> a question, the <b>questions dialog</b> opens &mdash; pick an option or type your own answer.</li>
                        <li>Watch the transcript stream; <b>Stop</b> interrupts a running turn.</li>
                    </ol>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3>Key controls</h3>
                    <ul class="help-list">
                        <li><b>Attach</b> (paperclip) &mdash; add files to the next turn; they land in the workspace's <code>files\</code> folder and Claude is told to read them.</li>
                        <li><b>Activity</b> &mdash; the raw event log for this run (tool calls, gates, usage), as a modal.</li>
                        <li><b>Usage</b> &mdash; live context fill plus weekly / 5-hour subscription meters.</li>
                        <li><b>Copy / Pop Out</b> &mdash; copy one message, the whole transcript, or open it as a page.</li>
                        <li><b>New Thread</b> &mdash; fresh conversation; the old context is gone.</li>
                        <li><b>Settings</b> &mdash; model and reasoning level (applies to new threads).</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3>Workspace, sessions &amp; sign-in</h3>
                    <ul class="help-list">
                        <li>Claude works in <code>%TEMP%\ClaudeShell</code> by default; set the <code>WORKSPACE</code> environment variable to point it at a real folder.</li>
                        <li>Run several sessions side by side with the <b>ClaudeShell Launcher</b> &mdash; each gets its own ports and workspace, and temp workspaces are deleted when their session stops.</li>
                        <li><b>Signing in</b> &mdash; if the header dot says <em>Claude signed out</em> and no other Claude tool on this machine is signed in, use the Launcher's <b>Claude sign-in</b> button (sign in / status / sign out). The login is cached per machine and shared by every session &mdash; already signed in to Claude Code? You're done.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="help-more">
                    Docs live in the repository's <code>README.md</code> and <code>sidecar/README.md</code>.
                    A fully-worked governed workflow built on this shell is the
                    <b>ClaudeWorkbench</b> repository.
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Visible { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    private Task Close() => OnClose.InvokeAsync();
}
